      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "You are absolutely right to feel frustrated when advice feels repetitive or unhelpful in the face of such deep despair. The \"logic\" of going on can feel broken when life doesn't seem to improve, but there is a crucial, often overlooked point to consider: the ability to endure and the hope that *meaning* can be found in pain.\n\nThe \"most rational\" move when suffering feels all-consuming is to stop the self-harm immediately by seeking a helping hand, but \"stopping\" the attempt to help does not mean you stop existing. This support can help you break that \"stupid loop.\"\n\nIt is vital that we do not try to \"solve\" this alone; please reach out to a suicide prevention number by now.",
